{{- /* chezmoi:modify-template */ -}}
{{- /*
  Selective field control for ~/.claude/settings.json.

  Why: Claude Code's /config slash command writes user-toggled settings
  (alwaysThinkingEnabled, useAutoModeDuringPlan, voiceEnabled, etc.) directly
  into ~/.claude/settings.json, which would create drift against any plain
  chezmoi template. There is no user-level ~/.claude/settings.local.json that
  Claude Code reads, so a clean split into local/shared isn't possible at the
  user scope.

  How: this is a chezmoi modify-template (https://www.chezmoi.io/user-guide/
  manage-different-types-of-file/#modify-templates). It receives the current
  ~/.claude/settings.json on .chezmoi.stdin, overlays the stable fields below
  via setValueAtPath, and writes the merged result back.

  Three categories of field, not two:

    STABLE       overwritten from here on every apply, whatever the live file
                 says: permissions, hooks, statusLine, skillOverrides,
                 cleanupPeriodDays, autoUpdatesChannel, remoteControlAtStartup.
    FREE-DRIFT   passed through untouched: alwaysThinkingEnabled, voiceEnabled,
                 useAutoModeDuringPlan and anything else /config adds.
    enabledPlugins  the ROSTER is fixed here and the per-plugin STATE is not.
                 Membership of the declared list is stable; a DECLARED plugin
                 the live file disables (JSON boolean false) or pins (JSON array
                 of version constraints) keeps that across applies. An
                 UNDECLARED one keeps nothing, the write is whole-value, so its
                 entry is erased. The price is that this repo no longer
                 re-asserts plugin state at all, and that a live disable is
                 invisible to `chezmoi status`, `chezmoi diff` and `just d`.
                 See the plugin block below.

  Promote a /config toggle to STABLE by adding it to one of the setValueAtPath
  calls below.
*/ -}}
{{- /* .chezmoi.stdin is only set when chezmoi runs the modify template
       with a real target file. Use safe access so the template still
       renders cleanly under `chezmoi execute-template` for ad-hoc testing.

       TRIMMED before the emptiness test, and that is a correctness
       requirement rather than tidiness. An empty string is falsy and a string
       of whitespace is not, so an untrimmed read sends a blank file to
       fromJson, which HARD ERRORS on it (`error calling fromJson: EOF`,
       measured 2026-08-02 on chezmoi 2.62.3 and 2.71.1). A modify-template
       that errors aborts the WHOLE apply, not just this target: every later
       target and every run_after_ script is skipped, and the corrupt file is
       left in place, so permissions.deny is not restored either. A file
       holding one newline is what an editor leaves after saving an emptied
       buffer, so this is the cheapest shape to produce.

       KNOWN LIMIT, deliberately not worked around here. Trimming only fixes
       the shapes that are EMPTY once trimmed. A live file that is non-empty
       and does not parse (a write truncated mid-object, a hand edit with a
       stray character) still aborts the apply, and no template can catch it:
       chezmoi's three JSON readers (fromJson, fromJsonc, fromYaml) all fail
       the template on bad input, and Go's text/template has no recover, so
       there is nothing to fall back FROM (measured 2026-08-02, and
       test/unit/claude-enabled-plugins.sh pins the boundary with a case per
       shape). Repairing that needs something outside this template that runs
       BEFORE it. Until then the apply's own error names this file. Repair
       ~/.claude/settings.json if you can. DELETING it loses the one managed
       thing this template cannot rebuild: plugin state is READ from the live
       file rather than declared here, so with nothing to read every declared
       plugin renders `true`, which re-enables every disabled plugin and drops
       every version pin. Nothing reports that afterwards either (see the plugin
       block below). Note the disabled set first and restore it with
       `claude plugin disable <id>` per plugin. Everything else this template
       manages does come back from here on the next apply, and free-drift keys
       are lost as before. */ -}}
{{- $stdin := index .chezmoi "stdin" | default "" | trim -}}
{{- $merged := dict -}}
{{- if $stdin -}}
{{-   $merged = fromJson $stdin -}}
{{- end -}}

{{- /* The live file's own enabledPlugins, read HERE so no setValueAtPath call
       below can overwrite it before the plugin block consumes it.

       Both containers are kind-guarded to a MAP before they are indexed, and
       that is a correctness requirement rather than caution. Measured
       2026-08-02 on chezmoi 2.62.3 and 2.71.1, which agreed on every idiom:
       `index` on an untyped nil is a HARD error, and `hasKey` is nil-safe but
       is a HARD error on a non-map (`wrong type for value; expected
       map[string]interface {}`). An unguarded read kills the WHOLE render, and
       chezmoi then writes no settings.json at all, taking permissions.deny,
       every hook, statusLine and every skillOverrides entry with it. Both
       containers legitimately arrive as something other than a map: the live
       file is absent or empty on a fresh machine, and enabledPlugins is JSON
       null once anything writes the key without entries. A nil check alone is
       not enough, which is why the guard tests for `map` rather than for
       presence. */ -}}
{{- $livePlugins := dict -}}
{{- if eq (kindOf $merged) "map" -}}
{{-   $liveEnabledPlugins := index $merged "enabledPlugins" -}}
{{-   if eq (kindOf $liveEnabledPlugins) "map" -}}
{{-     $livePlugins = $liveEnabledPlugins -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}

{{- /* --- stable: scalars and policy --- */ -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "cleanupPeriodDays" 36525 $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "autoUpdatesChannel" "stable" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "remoteControlAtStartup" true $merged -}}

{{- $permissions := dict
    "allow" (list
      "Read"
      "Grep"
      "Glob"
      "WebFetch"
      "WebSearch"
      "Bash(find *)"
      "Bash(cat *)"
      "Bash(ls *)"
      "Bash(head *)"
      "Bash(tail *)"
      "Bash(wc *)"
      "Bash(grep *)"
      "Bash(tree *)")
    "deny" (list
      "Read(.env)"
      "Read(.env.*)"
      "Read(secrets/**)"
      "Read(credentials.json)"
      "Read(.aws/credentials)"
      "Read(.ssh/id_*)")
    "defaultMode" "bypassPermissions" -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "permissions" $permissions $merged -}}

{{- /* --- stable: hooks (paths use $home for portability) --- */ -}}
{{- $home := .chezmoi.homeDir -}}
{{- $hooks := dict
    "UserPromptSubmit" (list (dict
      "hooks" (list (dict
        "type" "command"
        "command" (printf "%s/.local/bin/claude-user-prompt-start.sh" $home)))))
    "Stop" (list (dict
      "hooks" (list
        (dict
          "type" "command"
          "command" (printf "%s/.local/bin/claude-stop-pulse.sh" $home))
        (dict
          "type" "command"
          "async" true
          "command" (printf "%s/.local/bin/relay-agent.sh done" $home)))))
    "Notification" (list (dict
      "matcher" "permission_prompt"
      "hooks" (list
        (dict
          "type" "command"
          "command" "alerter --timeout 30 --title 'Claude Code' --message 'Needs attention' --sound default")
        (dict
          "type" "command"
          "async" true
          "command" (printf "%s/.local/bin/relay-agent.sh blocked" $home)))))
    "PostToolUse" (list
      (dict
        "matcher" "AskUserQuestion"
        "hooks" (list (dict
          "type" "command"
          "async" true
          "command" (printf "%s/.local/bin/relay-agent.sh asked" $home))))
      (dict
        "matcher" "ExitPlanMode"
        "hooks" (list (dict
          "type" "command"
          "async" true
          "command" (printf "%s/.local/bin/relay-agent.sh plan-ready" $home)))))
    "PreToolUse" (list (dict
      "matcher" "Bash"
      "hooks" (list (dict
        "type" "command"
        "command" (printf "%s/.local/bin/claude-audit.sh" $home))))) -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "hooks" $hooks $merged -}}

{{- /* --- stable: statusLine (path uses $home) --- */ -}}
{{- $statusLine := dict
    "type" "command"
    "command" (printf "bash %s/.claude/statusline-command.sh" $home) -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "statusLine" $statusLine $merged -}}

{{- /* --- the declared plugin ROSTER, ON by default, with the machine's own
       per-plugin STATE preserved. The roster is stable; the state is not.

       This block REPLACES enabledPlugins wholesale, it does not merge into it,
       because setValueAtPath writes the value at the path. So every entry the
       live file holds for an id missing from the list below is ERASED on the
       next apply, silently. Every MARKETPLACE plugin meant to stay on must be
       listed: Claude Code builds its marketplace-plugin load set out of these
       keys, so erasing an id stops that plugin loading (read out of the shipped
       2.1.220 binary on 2026-08-02). A plugin under ~/.claude/skills/ resolves
       the other way, its manifest default (ON) applies when no entry is
       present, so listing a skill is not what keeps it on and erasing a `false`
       for one REVOKES that disable. Those are not in this roster and are not
       meant to be. test/unit/claude-enabled-plugins.sh fails when this set and
       the roster disagree.

       The list is names only, not name-to-value pairs: membership means "this
       repo manages this plugin, and it is ON unless the machine already says
       something else". Claude Code 2.1.220's settings schema declares this key
       as `record(string, union([array(string), boolean, undefined]))`, and BOTH
       members of that union are the machine's to set, so both are carried
       through: a boolean (what `claude plugin disable <id>` writes, and the
       only supported way to stop a plugin's code running) and an array (what
       that schema calls the extended format with version constraints, a plugin
       held at a reviewed release). Every OTHER shape renders true, including
       absent, a JSON null, a string and a number, none of which enables
       anything on its own. Establishing the KIND before using the value is what
       keeps that safe: `eq X false` ERRORS whenever X is not a bool, measured
       2026-08-02, and a template error loses the whole file.

       Collapsing the array form to `true` would keep the plugin on and drop its
       pin, returning it to unconstrained. That fails in the direction that runs
       MORE code (ponytail ships JavaScript lifecycle hooks), so it is not the
       safe default it looks like. No CLI path is known to write the array form,
       so this branch may be unreachable in practice; it is written this way
       because the cost of being wrong is asymmetric.

       WHAT THIS GIVES UP, and it is more than the disable itself. Before this,
       the whole-value write forced every declared plugin back to `true` on
       every apply, so it incidentally RE-ASSERTED plugin state and remediated
       tampering. It no longer does. A live `false` is carried forward for as
       long as it sits in the file, and because the render reproduces it byte
       for byte, `chezmoi status` and `chezmoi diff` print NOTHING for it
       (measured 2026-08-02), which includes `just d`. So any process running as
       this user, which is every agent with Bash under
       `permissions.defaultMode = bypassPermissions`, permanently disables
       `security-guidance` or `superpowers` by writing one boolean, and nothing
       in this repo detects it or restores it. Re-enabling is a deliberate act
       too: `claude plugin enable <id>`, per plugin, and `claude plugin disable
       --all` has no `enable --all` counterpart, so recovering from a mass
       disable is one command per declared plugin. The trade goes this way
       because a containment verb a scheduled apply can silently revoke is not
       containment. It is a real cost, not a formality.

       The disable that sticks is against an APPLY, which is not the same as
       "the plugin cannot load". Settings precedence runs user < project <
       local < flag < policy, so a repo whose project settings enable the plugin
       loads it there regardless of this file; Claude Code has a dedicated
       `ineffective-disable` diagnostic for exactly that (both the diagnostic id
       and all five source names are in the shipped 2.1.220 binary, read
       2026-08-02).

       ponytail is a marketplace plugin rather than an official one: its
       marketplace is added separately (`claude plugin marketplace add
       DietrichGebert/ponytail`) and its entry only records that it should be
       ENABLED once installed. Enabling a plugin that is not installed is inert,
       so the declaration is safe on a fresh machine. --- */ -}}
{{- $declaredPlugins := list
    "superpowers@claude-plugins-official"
    "document-skills@anthropic-agent-skills"
    "frontend-design@claude-plugins-official"
    "playwright@claude-plugins-official"
    "security-guidance@claude-plugins-official"
    "swift-lsp@claude-plugins-official"
    "rust-analyzer-lsp@claude-plugins-official"
    "codex@openai-codex"
    "ponytail@ponytail" -}}
{{- /* No hasKey test: $livePlugins is a map by the guard above, so `index` on
       an absent key returns an untyped nil, whose kind is neither `bool` nor
       `slice`, so the value test below already covers absence. Measured
       2026-08-02 by replacing the hasKey call with a literal `true`: no case in
       test/unit/claude-enabled-plugins.sh changed verdict, which is what makes
       it dead rather than defensive. */ -}}
{{- $enabledPlugins := dict -}}
{{- range $pluginName := $declaredPlugins -}}
{{-   $pluginEnabled := true -}}
{{-   $liveValue := index $livePlugins $pluginName -}}
{{-   $liveValueKind := kindOf $liveValue -}}
{{-   if or (eq $liveValueKind "bool") (eq $liveValueKind "slice") -}}
{{-     $pluginEnabled = $liveValue -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{-   $enabledPlugins = set $enabledPlugins $pluginName $pluginEnabled -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "enabledPlugins" $enabledPlugins $merged -}}

{{- /* --- stable: skill tiering (on-demand skills load only when the user
       invokes them). Source of truth: the tiers table in
       dot_agents/custom-skill-lock.json, every on-demand skill gets exactly
       one entry here, core skills get none, and test/unit/skills-roster-fanout.sh
       fails the build when the two sets diverge. Per-key setValueAtPath (not
       one whole-dict overwrite) so overrides the user sets for other skills
       via /config pass through untouched. --- */ -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.cua-driver" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.elevenlabs" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.embedded-captions" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.faceless-explainer" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.general-video" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.home-assistant" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.home-assistant-best-practices" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.hyperframes" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.hyperframes-animation" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.hyperframes-cli" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.hyperframes-core" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.hyperframes-creative" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.hyperframes-keyframes" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.hyperframes-registry" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.kubernetes-specialist" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.last30days" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.lobster" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.media-use" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.motion-graphics" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.summarize-pro" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.tiktok-crawling" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.video-transcript-downloader" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}
{{- $merged = setValueAtPath "skillOverrides.website-to-video" "user-invocable-only" $merged -}}

{{ $merged | toPrettyJson }}
